<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18474" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφοσί-ωσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>purification, expiation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				2.52
			</span></i>: pl., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.302b
			</span></i>; defined as 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁσιότητος παραλ ελειμμένης ἀποπλήρωσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herm.
					<u>in Phdr.</u>
					p.94A.
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>doing as matter of form,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφοσιώσεως ἕνεκεν</span> for
			<i>form's</i> sake, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Eum.</u>
				12
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιμῆς ἀ.</span>
			<i>outward, formal</i> respect, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Tim.</u>
				39
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ ἀφοσίωσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dam.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					171
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
